    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0061" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.50/1–1749</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State for
                        Occupied Areas</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Saltzman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the united States Representative on the Far Eastern
                        Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McCoy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-08">February 8,
                        1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In accordance with previous oral instructions, and pursuant to the U.S. position
                    set forth in the final two paragraphs of your statement of December 9,
                        1948,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d24-f1"/> regarding “Excessive Concentration of
                    Economic Power in Japan”, it is requested that the U.S. Delegation oppose C
                    2–230/4, “Policy on Excessive Concentration of Economic Power”, and attempt to
                    dissuade FEC Members from giving further consideration to this or any other
                    proposal which would have as its purpose the development of additional policy on
                    the subject of excessive concentration of economic power in Japan. Should C
                    2–230/4 or a similar proposal be sent forward to the Commission, you should
                    prevent its adoption by the Commission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles</hi> E. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Saltzman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
